      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The step size is h=7/2-1=5/2. Both derivatives use the initial values (x,y,z)=(1,2,-2): y'=3-2-2=-1 and z'=2-6+2=-2. Thus Euler's method gives y(7/2)≈2+(5/2)(-1)=-1/2 and z(7/2)≈-2+(5/2)(-2)=-7. The mathematics is clear, but no Math Academy answer or grade for this question is captured; the supplied worked example concerns a different problem.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
          {
