        "question": {
          "dom_id": "step-q333276",
          "name": "Question 10",
          "problem": "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x):$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=x-y+{z}^{2},\\, & y(0)=1 \\\\ {z}^{′}=1-2y+3z,\\, & z(0)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(2)$ and $z(2).$\n\n$y(2)≈$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,z(2)≈$\n{{field-2}}",
          "worked_solution": "",
          "calculator_instructions": "",
