ath>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E86-MJMAIN-31\" d=\"M213 578L200 573Q186 568 160 563T102 556H83V602H102Q149 604 189 617T245 641T273 663Q275 666 285 666Q294 666 302 660V361L303 61Q310 54 315 52T339 48T401 46H427V0H416Q395 3 257 3Q121 3 100 0H88V46H114Q136 46 152 46T177 47T193 50T201 52T207 57T213 61V578Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E86-MJMAIN-29\" d=\"M60 749L64 750Q69 750 74 750H86L114 726Q208 641 251 514T294 250Q294 182 284 119T261 12T224 -76T186 -143T145 -194T113 -227T90 -246Q87 -249 86 -250H74Q66 -250 63 -250T58 -247T55 -238Q56 -237 66 -225Q221 -64 221 250T66 725Q56 737 55 738Q55 746 60 749Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E86-MJMAIN-2248\" d=\"M55 319Q55 360 72 393T114 444T163 472T205 482Q207 482 213 482T223 483Q262 483 296 468T393 413L443 381Q502 346 553 346Q609 346 649 375T694 454Q694 465 698 474T708 483Q722 483 722 452Q722 386 675 338T555 289Q514 289 468 310T388 357T308 404T224 426Q164 426 125 393T83 318Q81 289 69 289Q55 289 55 319ZM55 85Q55 126 72 159T114 210T163 238T205 248Q207 248 213 248T223 249Q262 249 296 234T393 179L443 147Q502 112 553 112Q609 112 649 141T694 220Q694 249 708 249T722 217Q722 153 675 104T555 55Q514 55 468 76T388 123T308 170T224 192Q164 192 125 159T83 84Q80 55 69 55Q55 55 55 85Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E86-MJMAIN-36\" d=\"M42 313Q42 476 123 571T303 666Q372 666 402 630T432 550Q432 525 418 510T379 495Q356 495 341 509T326 548Q326 592 373 601Q351 623 311 626Q240 626 194 566Q147 500 147 364L148 360Q153 366 156 373Q197 433 263 433H267Q313 433 348 414Q372 400 396 374T435 317Q456 268 456 210V192Q456 169 451 149Q440 90 387 34T253 -22Q225 -22 199 -14T143 16T92 75T56 172T42 313ZM257 397Q227 397 205 380T171 335T154 278T148 216Q148 133 160 97T198 39Q222 21 251 21Q302 21 329 59Q342 77 347 104T352 209Q352 289 347 316T329 361Q302 397 257 397Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E86-MJMAIN-2E\" d=\"M78 60Q78 84 95 102T138 120Q162 120 180 104T199 61Q199 36 182 18T139 0T96 17T78 60Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E86-MJMATHI-7A\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E86-MJMAIN-28\" x=\"468\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E86-MJMAIN-31\" x=\"858\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E86-MJMAIN-29\" x=\"1358\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E86-MJMAIN-2248\" x=\"2025\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<g transform=\"translate(3082,0)\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E86-MJMAIN-36\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E86-MJMAIN-2E\" x=\"500\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</g>\n</svg></span></p>\n<p>Notice that this component-wise approach is not specific to Euler's method. Indeed, we could apply any numerical method component-wise to approximate the solution to a system of ODEs!</p>\n           \n                </div>        \n                    \n            </div>",
